  "details": "Since October, when the new desktop HUD UI was brought over to the main branch, I've been experiencing a bug that has so far yet to have been fixed. The bug makes it so any actions that requires me to hold down a mouse button, and then physically drag said mouse, immediately results in VRChat forcing me to let go of that button upon movement of the mouse. It affects everything from VRChat's UI, in-world UI, items that require me to hold down a button to keep them in hand, VRChat's camera, etc. \n\nI have reported this bug in a previous report; however, that report was then merged into a bug report regarding clicks and actions being doubled. Although that bug was fixed, the own I've been experiencing has not. So far, I've yet to see anyone else possess this same bug that I have. All I know is that it affects me, regardless of any mouse or trackpad that I use. \n\nI am currently running VRChat on Linux Mint through Proton 9.0-4.",
